			],
			"Message": "docs(Rest): Rewrite doc comments across all modules with consistent structure\n\nStandardise Rust documentation throughout the entire Rest crate — module-level headers, function docs, struct/enum descriptions, and inline comments — to follow a uniform style:\n\n- Add `## Modules` lists to all parent module files (Fn/mod.rs, OXC/mod.rs, SWC/mod.rs, NLS/mod.rs, etc.) enumerating their sub-modules with one-line descriptions\n- Convert `//! Re-exports ...` module headers into proper module-level doc comments with `#`-prefixed section headings\n- Add structured `## Arguments`, `## Returns`, `## Errors`, `## Parameters`, and `## Panics` sections to all public functions\n- Normalise doc comment punctuation: complete sentences with trailing periods, consistent em-dash and code-fence formatting, proper definite articles\n- Remove redundant self-evident statements (\"This function does not panic.\", commented-out placeholder markers, trivial function descriptions)\n- Fix grammar and terminology: \"initialise\" → \"initialise\", hyphenation of compound modifiers, proper use of backtick-wrapped identifiers\n- Add `Config` method documentation with chaining-pattern descriptions for builder methods\n- Document safety invariants on `ParseResult` with the segfault-prevention explanation moved from a comment into structured doc\n- Add `#![allow(dead_code)]` and module-level attribution to Library.rs\n\nThese changes carry no runtime behaviour impact — only doc comments and inline documentation are modified across 36 source files.",
			"SHA": "d9d86d414a3ef056e99029cdebdc9cbc39fa377f"
		},
		{
