			"Message": "docs(Rest): Rebrand Rest from TypeScript compiler to HTTP/REST API server\n\nRewrite the entire README to reflect Rest's actual role as the HTTP/REST API server for the Land ecosystem, correcting a long-standing mismatch between project documentation and implementation.\n\nThe previous README described Rest as a high-performance TypeScript compiler built on OXC — a description that belonged to a different project phase. The new documentation accurately presents Rest as the backend API layer serving the Land web application, with:\n- Updated tagline, badges, and overview reflecting the HTTP server role\n- Architecture diagram showing Fn/ handler modules and Struct/ data types connected to Maintain and Cocoon\n- Full project structure tree documenting all Fn/, Struct/, and Binary/ modules\n- Getting Started section with correct build and library usage instructions\n- Compatibility table mapping Rest to its actual consumers (Maintain, Cocoon, Land Web App)\n- Updated API documentation link to the correct rest.editor.land subdomain\n\nThe emoji spacing convention (&#x2001;) is applied to all section headings for consistency with the project's formatting standards.",
